      "title": "hablara",
      "headword": "hablara",
      "romanization": "hablara",
      "gloss": "the form for supposing — carved out of a form you already own, with the only rule in Spanish that has no exceptions",
      "script": "latin",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:3b41c82064c4d8d6",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Give the they past of hablar, comer and vivir. (Hablaron, comieron, vivieron.)"
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "You were told those would be used twice. This is the second time."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "grammar",
          "title": "Grammar Lens: swap the ending",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Take the they past. Swap -ron for -ra."
            },
            {
              "kind": "table",
              "headers": [
                "they past",
                "supposing"
              ],
              "columns": 2,
              "rowCount": 3,
              "utterances": [
                "they past: hablaron. supposing: hablara.",
                "they past: comieron. supposing: comiera.",
                "they past: vivieron. supposing: viviera."
              ]
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "No verb in Spanish changes its stem here — a stronger guarantee than almost anything else in the language. The one thing the swap does not carry is an accent: habláramos, tuviéramos. The stem is untouched; only the mark moves."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The reason is worth a moment: every irregularity these verbs had was already spent in the preterite. Because this form is carved out of that one, it inherits the irregularity instead of inventing new irregularity. A tense built on a broken form comes out perfectly regular."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Hablara did not start out as supposing."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "In Latin this ending was a plain statement about the past: amāveram, I had loved. It slid from what had happened to what did not, which is a short journey — both sit outside the present, and only one is real."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "(Hablar's Latin ancestor was deponent, so Spanish built hablara on the pattern rather than inheriting it. The ending carried over, not the word.)"
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Spanish also has a second form for exactly this job — hablase — and that one did come from a Latin subjunctive. Two different Latin tenses walked into the same modern meaning. You will meet -se in reading; you never have to produce it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
